    "institutions_today": [],
    "paragraph": "\"Protective accessibility for resilient urban mobility under recurrent air threats\" introduces the Protective Shelter Accessibility Index to measure pedestrian access from public transit stops to emergency shelters across varying walking horizons. Combining Tokyo mobile phone mobility data with multi-year firm transaction records, \"Physical co-presence of workers is linked with the evolution of interfirm networks\" assesses how worker encounter opportunities relate to economic tie formation. Finally, \"Statistical and Machine Learning Approaches for Estimating Visitation to Natural Spaces in the UK\" develops statistical and machine learning models to predict visitor counts in green and blue spaces across England and Wales.",
